{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "scale-county-timeagg-year-minor-running-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.74, step 7f. `scale-county-timeagg-year-minor-running`: `scale-county-timeagg-year`'s Year collapse (January, April, July and October 2020, both day types, all 24 hours, source types 21 and 62, `inputs/washtenaw-county-timeagg.esm`, VMT output on) on road type 4 alone, selecting `scale-county-minor-running`'s species unchanged: the PM species and PAH particles at running and crankcase running exhaust (1, 15), and the metals and dioxins/furans at running exhaust. MOVESOutput is 11,704 rows, the Hour twin's key set, and no metal or dioxin row.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES is the Hour twin's arithmetic over PreAggYEAR.sql's month collapse -- SulfatePMCalculator's pmSpeciation outputs, TOM, the residual and crankcase running's split from running exhaust's species, AirToxicsCalculator's PAH particles -- and the metals' and dioxins' absence at Year.\n\n`n_aggregatesMonths` is 1; `db_aggregationmonth` and `db_rateday` are read from its XML by `tools/runspec-month-selection.py` and `tools/runspec-day-selection.py`. `n_outputRate` is bound to 11704; `n_physicsRow` 21, the two source types' physics rows.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "single-county-domain",
      "running-exhaust",
      "crankcase",
      "pm-speciation",
      "air-toxics",
      "time-aggregation"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
